[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2767538847","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104772#issuecomment-2767538847","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104772","id":2767538847,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6k9Uqf","user":{"login":"ajreckof","id":66184050,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2MTg0MDUw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66184050?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ajreckof","html_url":"https://github.com/ajreckof","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ajreckof/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ajreckof/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ajreckof/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ajreckof/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ajreckof/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ajreckof/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ajreckof/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ajreckof/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ajreckof/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-31T22:15:33Z","updated_at":"2025-03-31T22:18:33Z","body":"The issue seems deeper then just about null. In particular it looks like if there is a contradiction between the type of the typed dictionary and the type of the value it will choose to follow the type of the value while it should follow the type of the dictionarry. \r\nHence I think the fix should try and address this behaviour.\r\n\r\nEdit : You can try and take example on how it is done for the array","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2767538847/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2770338788","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104772#issuecomment-2770338788","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104772","id":2770338788,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6lIAPk","user":{"login":"CreatedBySeb","id":11736217,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzM2MjE3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11736217?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb","html_url":"https://github.com/CreatedBySeb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-01T18:26:12Z","updated_at":"2025-04-01T18:26:12Z","body":"@ajreckof There is definitely some weirdness with how the typed dictionaries are handled and how they interact with different export annotations, in some cases there isn't an obvious expectation (e.g. how should `@export_enum` be handled, should it be the key or the value that is the enum, or should it be unsupported entirely?) However I think a more thorough overhaul of this code would be out of scope for a bug fix or a patch version change, it would probably need some discussion and be included into the next 4.x release.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2770338788/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2770443873","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104772#issuecomment-2770443873","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104772","id":2770443873,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6lIZ5h","user":{"login":"ajreckof","id":66184050,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2MTg0MDUw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66184050?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ajreckof","html_url":"https://github.com/ajreckof","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ajreckof/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ajreckof/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ajreckof/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ajreckof/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ajreckof/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ajreckof/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ajreckof/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ajreckof/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ajreckof/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-01T19:11:32Z","updated_at":"2025-04-01T19:11:50Z","body":"> @ajreckof There is definitely some weirdness with how the typed dictionaries are handled and how they interact with different export annotations, in some cases there isn't an obvious expectation (e.g. how should `@export_enum` be handled, should it be the key or the value that is the enum, or should it be unsupported entirely?).\n\nI fully agree with you that there are some weird case on type hints and other export stuffs but I. The contrary on the actual type there is no problem as they are fully given separately. Here you are fixing a problem of type mismatch (null where it should be resource) by modifying how a core function on a specific case. What I think you should do is take the problem one step back so that what is calling this function call it with the right value which should be Resource since it is typed as a Resource. \nThere are two reasons you should it this way. First the function you are modifying as way more reach then what you are trying to fix by modifying you might create bugs in other places that are hard to find.\nSecond you would only fix the issue for one specific case of type mismatch while this can happen for other reasons. One such case is changing the type in the script.\n\n> However I think a more thorough overhaul of this code would be out of scope for a bug fix or a patch version change, it would probably need some discussion and be included into the next 4.x release.\n\nI agree that a huge overall wouldn't be good for cherry picking but what I'm asking is just modifying the value that is given to the function you are modifying so that it never reaches the case you are handling. This would avoid touching a core function and reduce the scope of the modification giving it more chance to be cherry-picked.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2770443873/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2770751799","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104772#issuecomment-2770751799","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104772","id":2770751799,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6lJlE3","user":{"login":"CreatedBySeb","id":11736217,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzM2MjE3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11736217?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb","html_url":"https://github.com/CreatedBySeb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CreatedBySeb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-01T21:42:27Z","updated_at":"2025-04-01T21:42:27Z","body":"Sorry I think I misunderstood what you originally meant. I've found the better solution you were referring to in `EditorPropertyDictionary::update_property`, where I have it prioritise using the explicit value type rather than inferring it for the existing fields. This seems to still create the desired UX, and corrects the defect in the dictionary code rather than adding a workaround in the more general component. Thanks for the feedback!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2770751799/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2790994114","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104772#issuecomment-2790994114","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104772","id":2790994114,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6mWzDC","user":{"login":"CreatedBySeb","id":11736217,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzM2MjE3","